      "text": "The given function is $f(x) = \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1-x}{1+x}$. We need to find all the numbers in the range of this function.\n\nFirst, we use the tangent addition formula for the arctangent function:\n\\[\n\\arctan A + \\arctan B = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{A + B}{1 - AB} \\right)\n\\]\nprovided that $AB < 1$ for all valid arguments. Here, let \\( A = x \\) and \\( B = \\frac{1-x}{1+x} \\). Then,\n\\[\nAB = x \\cdot \\frac{1-x}{1+x} = \\frac{x(1-x)}{1+x} = \\frac{x - x^2}{1+x}.\n\\]\nWe need to check the condition \\( AB < 1 \\):\n\\[\n\\frac{x - x^2}{1 + x} < 1.\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\(1 + x\\) (which is positive for all \\( x \\neq -1 \\)),\n\\[\nx - x^2 < 1 + x \\implies -x^2 < 1 \\implies x^2 > -1.\n\\]\nThis inequality is always true, so the condition \\( AB < 1 \\) is satisfied for all real numbers \\( x \\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1-x}{1+x} = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x + \\frac{1-x}{1+x}}{1 - x \\cdot \\frac{1-x}{1+x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x + \\frac{1-x}{1+x}}{1 - \\frac{x(1-x)}{1+x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x + \\frac{1-x}{1+x}}{1 - \\frac{x - x^2}{1+x}} \\right).\n\\]\nSimplifying the expression inside the arctangent function, we get\n\\[\n\\arctan \\left( \\frac{x + \\frac{1-x}{1+x}}{1 - \\frac{x - x^2}{1+x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{\\frac{x(1+x) + (1-x)}{1+x}}{\\frac{1+x - (x - x^2)}{1+x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{\\frac{x + x^2 + 1 - x}{1+x}}{\\frac{1+x - x + x^2}{1+x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{\\frac{1 + x^2 + 1}{1+x}}{\\frac{1 + x^2}{1+x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{1 + x^2 + 1}{1 + x^2} \\right) = \\arctan(1).\n\\]\nSince \\(\\arctan(1) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\), we have\n\\[\nf(x) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n\\]\nThus, the function \\( f(x) \\) outputs only the value \\(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\) for all \\( x \\). Therefore, the range of the function is\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}.\n\\]",
