      "text": "For \\( f(x) = \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} \\), we start by using the identity for the sum of arctangents:    \n\\[ \\arctan a + \\arctan b = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{a + b}{1 - ab} \\right) \\quad \\text{if} \\quad ab < 1. \\]\nIn our case, let \\( a = x \\) and \\( b = \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} \\).\n\nFirst, we compute \\( ab \\):\n\\[ ab = x \\cdot \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x(1 - x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{x - x^2}{1 + x}. \\]\nWe need to determine the condition under which \\( ab < 1 \\):\n\\[ \\frac{x - x^2}{1 + x} < 1 \\]\n\\[ x - x^2 < 1 + x \\]\n\\[ -x^2 < 1 \\]\n\\[ x^2 > -1. \\]\nSince this inequality is always true for all real \\( x \\), we proceed with the arctangent identity:\n\\[ \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x}}{1 - x \\cdot \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x}} \\right). \\]\nSimplify the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[ x + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x(1 + x) + (1 - x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{x + x^2 + 1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x}. \\]\n\\[ 1 - x \\cdot \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{(1 + x) - x(1 - x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{1 + x - x + x^2}{1 + x} = \\frac{1 + x^2}{1 + x}. \\]\nThus,\n\\[ \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{\\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x}}{\\frac{1 + x^2}{1 + x}} \\right) = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x^2} \\right). \\]\nNotice that:\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x^2} = 1. \\]\nTherefore,\n\\[ \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x^2} \\right) = \\arctan 1 = \\frac{\\pi}{4}. \\]\nHence, the range of \\( f(x) \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}. \\]",
